# Volume One

*A shorter account of what shows up when you look*

## Part 1. What seems to be the case

Most of the time nothing extra is required. The cup is for drinking. The car is for going. That way of being with things can stay as it is. This book does not turn living into homework.

Sometimes you pause anyway — not always with a large question. Sometimes it is only: what is this, really? You are no longer only living with it. That pause is why the pages below exist. You can skip them and drink. If you stay, here is what a look seems to need, and what it has to leave out.

Once a look has started, some things seem to hold. The sections below name them. They belong to one look, written in pieces so they can be read one at a time.

### What “look” means here

Look means you have stopped only living with the thing and started asking what holds the way you named it. A glance is not required. A theory of the universe is not required. People use other words for that moment — knowing, analyzing, being certain. This book will say *look*, then stop announcing the choice.

If numbers show up later, they are marks on this look. They are not the cup, the sum, or the meaning. A moral claim, a proof, a “how do I know,” a “what is it like” can each be a this. The book is not an ethics, a logic, a theory of knowledge, or a study of experience. It will look at those the way it looks at a cup.

### Once a look has started

If a look has started, you do not first have to decide what the world is made of. Matter, mind, God, a simulation, turtles all the way down — any of those might be true, or none of them. Almost anything could be going on, including nothing you could use. The look still starts on something already here. A cup on the table. A number on a page.

That open space is not a picture of the universe. It is only this: the look has not first picked a world-picture. There is no guarantee that the world is tidy, or that it will hold still. The look proceeds anyway, without that promise.

You can look at any of those world-pictures later, as a line of its own at the top of a page. You do not have to pick one in order to look at the cup.

*The look starts in the middle. You have not first chosen what the world is made of. The cup is already on the table.*

Someone will say: then you are only describing looking, so you are saying nothing. This is not a claim that the cup is only a look. It is a claim about what a look needs, and what a look has to leave out.

### A cup on the table — picture first

Before more names, here is what a finished page can look like. You wrote at the top: *There is a cup on the table.* Some of what came forward helps that sentence stay standing. Some of it showed up and does not.

| What came forward | none | weak | some | strong |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| The shape you can hold |  |  |  | ● |
| That you can drink from it |  |  |  | ● |
| The word *cup* |  |  | ● |  |
| Other cups you have used |  |  | ● |  |
| Heat in the hand if there is coffee |  |  | ● |  |
| Steam above the coffee | ● |  |  |  |
| A factory rumor, somewhere cups are made | ● |  |  |  |

A short list is enough. Five is plenty. This page lists seven because steam and a factory rumor showed up. You do not have to hunt for seven.

Shape, drinking, and other cups sit together as one picture of the cup you named. The word *cup* sits nearby. Heat sits nearby when there is coffee. Steam above the coffee, and a factory rumor, came forward and do not join. “Cups exist in themselves” never came forward on this page. That stays off the sheet.

The list is not the cup. Living already had a cup. This page makes a cup-under-a-look. And one more line at the bottom: this look is not the world. The drink is still there.

Keep that picture. Next we name what you already saw. Then two small permissions: you can swap the middle line, and you can look inside one of the things that hold it.

You will see this page again, blank, when it is your turn.

Later you can write the line another way and run the same questions. The sky will still be the sky. Stadium lights can change what holds. Same world. Different line at the top. That is a second look. The worksheet is how you get there without a machine.

**Four names that do not trade places**

From the cup page, four working names are enough:

|  |  |
| --- | --- |
| **What you wrote** | The line at the top. The cup-sentence, or whatever you named. The middle of the page. |
| **What holds it** | Listed things that point back — that help the sentence you wrote stay standing. |
| **What showed up and does not** | Listed things that came forward and do not hold that sentence up. Call this *leftover* once the pile is clear. |
| **The rim** | One line: this look is not the world. |

A line points back when it helps the sentence you wrote stay standing. Picture a hand under the cup: the shape of the cup holds the cup-sentence up; steam on this page does not.

• **Strong** means it points back hard.

• **Weak** means it barely does.

• **Some** means it points back partway — between strong and weak.

• **None** means it came forward and does not hold the line up. That is leftover.

Leftover is not a defect. It is not a hidden substance sitting in the ceramic.

Three piles stay distinct. They must not trade places:

• **Leftover** — what you listed that does not hold the line up, this time.

• **Unlisted** — what never came forward. Off the sheet. Do not hunt it. Hunting it turns living into homework.

• **Rim** — one line on the page: this look is not the world. That line is not leftover, and it is not Unlisted. Do not turn the rim into a third leftover list.

After that first definition, leftover can stand alone.

### This against that

If there is a look, there has to be contrast. What you wrote only shows as that line because something else is not it. Heat against the word *cup* can sit in the same scene. Steam can show up and still refuse to join, if all you wrote down was that there is a cup on the table.

You do not need a country called Non-Existence for contrast to work. “Not the cup” is enough.

### What holds

Once there is difference, some of it connects. Some of what came forward points back to what you named. Some of it stops short.

The things that hold the sentence are not the cup. Putting them together in this look is what makes it the examined cup. Change that putting-together and you have not smashed the ceramic. You have changed the look.

Until something sits in the middle and others sit with it, you only have a scene and some differences in the scene. Once both are there, you can ask what is holding the line at the top.

### What sits in the middle can change

On the page, one line sits in the middle. The other lines either hold that line up or they do not. Next time you can swap them. The word *cup* can sit in the middle, and the object on the table can be one of the things that hold it. Same room. Different middle.

### You can look inside one of the things that hold

What holds the cup is built the same way. Heat, if you open it, is held by a warm hand, a word for warmth, a burned mouth. You can look inside one of the things that hold. You can keep going. You do not have to. You can drink instead.

You do not have to settle whether it is holding all the way down, or turtles, before you look at the cup. Nesting is allowed. It is not required.

### Putting them together

Some of what came forward lines up with what you wrote down. Some of it does not. The shape you can hold may feel more like the cup you named. A factory rumor, if it came forward at all, may feel less like it. Steam may sit nearby and still refuse to hold the sentence up. Noticing that much is already a kind of measuring.

The noticing is a reading of this look. It is not a verdict on the world. It is not an average sitting on the page.

Someone will say: so looking made the cup.

No. Living already had a cup. The look makes a cup-under-a-look.

Someone will say: so there is a mysterious outside.

No realm was found. If you look at “the outside,” it enters what you wrote and is no longer outside. You just drew a bigger page. The rim is still there: this look is not the world.

Someone will say: who decides, so anything goes. For this look, what holds is what points back to what you wrote down. Write it down another way and you get a different set of marks. No referee sits above two honest looks. You pick the marks. Two honest looks can disagree.

### You can stop

You can keep looking. You can look inside one of the things that hold. You can look at the looking. Or you can go drink. The book does not follow you home.

## Part 2. A page you can use

If Part 1 is right, a look can be run on one line you write down. A pen is enough. A machine is not required. This is not a new method. It is the same look, written down.

The first half of this part shows how the page works. Then comes a blank page you can copy or tear out. After that, the same page already filled in, so the blanks have a body. Then a sum, and the sky-and-stadium second look.

### What this look is looking at

Write down what this look is looking at. That writing is the middle of the page. It does not have to be a sentence.

What you write can be a word, a sentence, a paragraph, a picture, a dance, a clip, a book. It can be an idea, an object, a feeling, an experience, a sensation, an intuition. If you need one cover-word for all of those, *expression* will do. If *thing* sits better in your hand, use that.

You write it down so the page has a middle. You have not turned a dance into a sentence. You have named what sits at the top.

“There is a cup on the table” is one look. “There is a cup on the table because we scored” is a different look. Same cup. Different line at the top.

What comes forward is asked to point back at what you wrote. A short list is enough. Five is plenty. What did not come forward stays off the page — unlisted. It is not leftover, and it is not the rim. Do not hunt it.

The rim is one line: this look is not the world.

### The short card

If you want the whole method in four lines:

|  |  |
| --- | --- |
| 1 | What is this? |
| 2 | What is holding it up? |
| 3 | What came forward and does not hold? |
| 4 | This look is not the world. |

Then the exit, which is not the rim: look again, or go live?

If that is all that gets used, that is enough. The longer page is the same four names, slower.

### How to fill the page

Title the page with what you are looking at. Write it again so it is sitting there. List what came forward. A short list is enough.

Mark each one none, weak, some, or strong. If this look wants numbers, use 0, 1, 2, or 3. Those are the same four rungs written as digits. Use one ladder on a line, not both.

Now look only at the ones that still point back — the ones you marked weak, some, or strong. Leave the ones marked none to the leftover pile. They have a different role on the page.

Among the ones that still hold, do they sit together as one picture of what you wrote down, or do two of them clash? They can be unlike and still hold. If two of the things that hold clash, circle those two and leave it at that. A clash among what holds is not leftover. Leftover is the pile that did not hold.

Write the rim as one line. Do not make a third leftover list there.

Someone has to pick the marks. This page will say you, because you are the one holding the pen. If it helps to call yourself a person, do that. This book does not know what a person is, and it does not need to. The marks belong to this look. Two honest looks can disagree. The sheet is not a judge.

### How to read what you wrote

When the page is full, look at it. One pile is holding the line up. The other pile came forward and did not join. See both piles at once. That seeing — both piles at once — is what this page means by tension. It is not a number under the piles.

Do not mash “how many held” and “how many did not” into one score and treat that number as what the cup means.

If you used the numbers, you can count how many listed things held and how many did not. Those two counts can sit next to each other. They are still two facts. They are not a score for the cup, the sum, or the sky. Then look again with a rewritten line at the top, or go live.

